t":null,"lat":42.42575,"lng":18.770889,"price":null,"priceClass":null,"hours":null,"url":null,"phone":null,"address":null,"content":"The biggest Orthodox church in the Old Town.","wikidata":"Q26696607"},{"type":"see","name":"Maritime Museum","alt":null,"lat":42.4252,"lng":18.771361,"price":"€4","priceClass":null,"hours":"Mon-Sat 08:00-20:00; Sun 09:00-13:00","url":null,"phone":"+382 32 304720","address":null,"content":"3 floors of photographs, uniforms, weapons, paintings, and model ships.","wikidata":"Q16677924"},{"type":"see","name":"Castle of San Giovanni","alt":"St John's Fortress","lat":42.422117,"lng":18.774816,"price":"15€","priceClass":null,"hours":null,"url":null,"phone":null,"address":null,"content":"Ruins of a castle at the top of the trail running along the fortifications of the town. Offers panoramic views of the walled town with the Bay of Kotor in the background.","wikidata":null},{"type":"see","name":"Church of Our Lady of Remedy","alt":"Crkva Gospe od Zdravlja","lat":42.424286,"lng":18.773204,"price":null,"priceClass":null,"hours":null,"url":null,"phone":null,"address":null,"content":"Church on the slopes of the mountain overlooking Kotor. Built in the 16th century by plague survivors to honor the Holy Mother. Accessed by climbing the trail up the fortifications from the old town.","wikidata":"Q4981066"},{"type":"see","name":"Aquarium Boka","alt":null,"lat":42.43616,"lng":18.76429,"price":"Adults €10, children (aged 6-18) €6, concessions €7","priceClass":null,"hours":"10:00-21:00 daily","url":"https://www.aquariumboka.ucg.ac.me/en/","phone":"+382 67 946497","address":"Put I Bokeljske brigade 68","content":"Small aquarium featuring entirely local marine species. Panel descriptions are in both Montenegrin and English.","wikidata":null},{"type":"do","name":"Stroll on the wall around Kotor","alt":null,"lat":null,"lng":null,"price":null,"priceClass":null,"hours":null,"url":null,"phone":null,"address":null,"content":"This is a nice evening or day walk. Take a rest, enjoy the view or bring some food and drinks.","wikidata":null},{"type":"do","name":"Boat Trips","alt":null,"lat":null,"lng":null,"price":null,"priceClass":null,"hours":null,"url":null,"phone":null,"address":null,"content":"In the middle of the bay there are two islands, (St. George Island) and (Our Lady of the Rocks), which are worth seeing and accessible by tourist boats (€15), which leave from outside the old town main gate. It is however much cheaper to first go by bus to Perast (€1) and then use a water taxi (€5) to get to the islands.","wikidata":null},{"type":"do","name":"Climb up inside the Fortress","alt":null,"lat":42.423611,"lng":18.771944,"price":"€15","priceClass":null,"hours":null,"url":null,"phone":null,"address":null,"content":"The fortifications are some 4.5 km away, directly above the walled city, on almost vertical cliffs. Upon reaching the fortress, you will be rewarded with a view of Kotor and the bay. Entry is advisable only for relatively physically fit people. Pay to use one of several entrances in the old city (near either the north or south gates) to climb up the 1,350 steps along switchbacks. The path is in relatively good shape,","wikidata":"Q12907852"},{"type":"do","name":"Climb up outside the Fortress","alt":null,"lat":42.42714,"lng":18.77378,"price":null,"priceClass":null,"hours":null,"url":null,"phone":null,"address":null,"content":"Alternatively, if you wish to skip the €15 and still be rewarded with a similar view, there is a trail behind the old power station, outside the city near the north gate, which runs parallel northeast of the fortifications. To find this trail (see GPS for starting point), exit the old walled city through the north gate, cross the bridge, and continue until the intersection with the main road. Then, make a right turn ","wikidata":null},{"type":"do","name":"Hike to Mausoleum of Njegoš","alt":null,"lat":42.399722,"lng":18.8375,"price":null,"priceClass":null,"hours":null,"url":null,"phone":null,"address":null,"content":"This is a full-day hike continuing further outside of the fortification, passing a zip-line, a nice little restaurant half-way, and into Lovćen National Park. Just 13 km, but from 0 m to 1,700 m of elevation.","wikidata":null},{"type":"eat","name":"Forza","alt":null,"lat":null,"lng":null,"price":null,"priceClass":"budget","hours":null,"url":null,"phone":null,"address":null,"content":"The most popular pastry shop in Kotor.","wikidata":null},{"type":"eat","name":"Pizzeria Pronto","alt":"Пиззериа Пронто","lat":null,"lng":null,"price":null,"priceClass":"budget","hours":null,"url":"https://www.facebook.com/Caffe-Pizzeria-Pronto-344435836209301/","phone":"+382 67 991 666","address":null,"content":"When you're ready for that big slice, come here and get one for €3.","wikidata":null},{"type":"eat","name":"Fish Grill","alt":null,"lat":null,"lng":null,"price":"Less than €10 for one meal","priceClass":"budget","hours":"Closed on Sun","url":"https://fish-grill-kotor.business.site/","phone":null,"address":null,"content":"Fresh fish and seafood cooked to order. Take away only. Various side dishes available, such as seafood risotto and fries/chips. Highly advisable to order in advance for the next day because quantities are very limited and might not be available if you show up without an advance order.","wikidata":null},{"type":"eat","name":"Sladoja Mesara Meat Shop & Grill","alt":null,"lat":null,"lng":null,"price":"Less than €5 for one meal","priceClass":"budget","hours":"Closed on Sunday","url":"https://sladoja.business.site/","phone":null,"address":null,"content":"Butcher shop with fresh meats cooked to order. Take away only. Various sides available, including grilled vegetables and fries/chips. Two grilled skewers with meat and vegetables for €3. -Google says closed. Have not confirmed in person","wikidata":null},{"type":"eat","name":"Pizzeria \"POCUO\"","alt":null,"lat":null,"lng":null,"price":"Dish of the day for less than €5","priceClass":"budget","ho